ISOLATING THE FACTOR: charge -1 with ONE term vs TWO terms (radial multiplicity)
                           pattern          charges   m0   M*  M*/m0 mult at busiest charge
      [Z^q,W,ZW]  q=4  (chg -1 x1)       [-1, 0, 4]    5    5   1.00          1
         [Z^4,W,ZW^2]  (chg -1 x2)          [-1, 4]    5   10   2.00          2
   [Z^4,W,ZW^3]  (chg -1 x2 wider)      [-2, -1, 4]    5    5   1.00          1
         [Z^3,W,ZW^2]  (chg -1 x2)          [-1, 3]    4    8   2.00          2
         [Z^2,W,ZW^2]  (chg -1 x2)          [-1, 2]    3    6   2.00          2
         [Z^5,W,ZW^2]  (chg -1 x2)          [-1, 5]    6   12   2.00          2

  If M*/m0 = 2 exactly when a charge carries 2 terms and = 1 when 1 term,
  the factor is RADIAL MULTIPLICITY (# terms sharing a charge), NOT the prime 2.
